    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d511">

                <pb facs="0514" n="1248" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1248"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mavroyeni Bey.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-04-05"><hi rendition="#italic">April 5,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 9.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Acknowledging the receipt of the note with
                    which you have favored me under to-day’s date, I have the pleasure to inform you
                    that the report of the intended visit of the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >San Francisco</hi> to Smyrna is correct. Having recently visited Jaffa, and
                    gone thence td the Piraeus and Palermo to await her consort, the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Marblehead</hi>, the two ships are about to cruise in
                    the Levant, a part of the Mediterranean which I trust may be more frequently the
                    scene of these friendly visits than has heretofore been practicable.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
